{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization.hasDerivAt_S_at_qstar_oneInstanton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization.hasDerivAt_S_at_qstar_oneInstanton","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OneInstantonNormalization.lean#L86-L99","doc":"**Consequence: the geometric `S`-slope at `q*` is `M(q*)·Z′ / u(q*)³`, exact.**\nChaining the realization into `BarOddLadderShape.hasDerivAt_S_at_qstar`: the\none-instanton lever slope at `q*` is the pure static lever with the amplitude\nlog-derivative dropping out — the committed exactness, now with the numerator slope\ngiven geometrically as amplitude × phase-slope. The open magnitude check is\n`M(q*)·Z′ = A′ ≈ +2.37`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization.barOddLadderShape_of_oneInstanton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization.barOddLadderShape_of_oneInstanton","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OneInstantonNormalization.lean#L66-L84","doc":"**The one-instanton Im form realizes a `BarOddLadderShape`.** Given the\none-instanton structure — a differentiable amplitude `M` (the smooth\n`𝒜_K·e^{−Re𝔙/πℏ}·prefactor`), an Im-phase factor `Z` with a simple zero at `q*`\n(`Z(q*) = 0`, slope `Z′`), a positive combined numerator slope `M(q*)·Z′ > 0`, and the\npositive ladder lever `u` — the categorical meridian numerator `A = M·Z` and its lever\n`S = A/u³` inhabit `BarOddLadderShape` with `A′ = M(q*)·Z′`. This is the geometric\nrealization `BarOddLadderShape` names as open, *conditional on* the one-instanton\nstructure holding for the actual `𝔙_q` (not proved here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization.numerator_hasDerivAt_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OneInstantonNormalization.numerator_hasDerivAt_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OneInstantonNormalization.lean#L54-L64","doc":"**The one-instanton numerator slope is log-derivative-free at the simple zero.**\nFor `A = M·Z` with `M` differentiable and `Z` vanishing at `q*`, the derivative at\n`q*` is `M(q*)·Z′(q*)` — the `M′·Z` term is killed by `Z(q*) = 0`. This is the\nproduct-rule content behind `BarOddLadderShape.hasDerivAt_S_at_qstar`'s \"zero\nlog-derivative correction\": the smooth exponential amplitude `M`'s own slope drops out\nat the zero. ","signatureChunk":0}]}